.TH AURORA 1 "October 2026" "vaevictis-aurora 1.1.0" "VaeVictis OS"
.SH NAME
aurora \- simple offline music player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aurora
[\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Aurora is the music player of VaeVictis OS. It keeps a library and playlists,
and has search, shuffle, repeat, playback speed and a real-time spectrum that
follows the music. Files given on the command line are added to the library and
played. If Aurora is already running, the running copy is brought to the front.
.PP
Aurora makes no network connection.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Qt platform to use. The default is "wayland;xcb". Set it to
.B xcb
to run through X11, for example to find out whether blurry text comes from
fractional scaling on Wayland.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.aurora/library.db
The library and the playlists (SQLite).
.TP
.I ~/.aurora/icon.svg
Optional window icon.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/linuxtuts-website/vaevictis-os
